{
  "$comment": "Paths that belong to ONE machine, and the inventory of every versioned file that still carries one. A path like this is not a secret, it is worse for this repository's purpose: it is a number that cannot be reproduced. bench/runs/ publishes the prompts a harness was given as evidence a reader can re-run, and 614 of those lines name a scratchpad that existed on one laptop, in one session. The list below is a ratchet: an entry may shrink or disappear, never grow, and a file that is not listed must carry none at all.",
  "$comment_patterns": "The same five shapes that scripts/gates/lib/external_crosscheck.py already calls MACHINE_PATHS. They are written here, once, so that the definition has one home rather than one per consumer. A bare /tmp/ is deliberately absent: bench/cases/cli-packer plants a predictable-temporary-file defect, and a rule that hunted it would go red on a faithful recording of a tool quoting that very line.",
  "$comment_self_exemption": "This file is the only thing excluded from the sweep, because it is the only file whose job is to spell the shapes out. gate-machine-identity.selftest.sh proves the exemption is not a hole: it writes this file's exact bytes into a neighbouring path and requires the gate to go red.",
  "$comment_expected_on_merge": "Files that carry one of these shapes for a legitimate reason and live on an open branch rather than here. Measured on 2026-09-11 across all seven open loop branches: these three are the whole set, and without declaring them this gate would go red the moment those branches merge - a defect no single branch can see, which is the exact class that cost iteration 7 an 80-minute chain run to find. Each entry names the branch it comes from, and the branch is verified when the checkout has that ref; a checkout that does not is reported as unverified rather than passed.",
  "self_exemption": "scripts/gates/data/machine-identity.json",
  "patterns": [
    "/Users/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+",
    "/home/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+",
    "/private/(?:tmp|var)/",
    "/var/folders/",
    "[A-Za-z]:\\\\\\\\?Users\\\\\\\\?"
  ],
  "expected_on_merge": {
    "scripts/gates/gate-budget-ledger.sh": {
      "occurrences": 1,
      "branch": "origin/loop/iter4-freshness-and-corpus",
      "why": "line 374 iterates over a synthetic prefix to prove the reference-frame fix; the prefix is invented, not a machine"
    },
    "scripts/gates/gate-external-crosscheck.selftest.sh": {
      "occurrences": 1,
      "branch": "origin/loop/iter7-external-tool-crosscheck",
      "why": "plants an invented account in an adapted finding as payload, so the crosscheck can be seen rejecting it"
    },
    "scripts/gates/lib/external_crosscheck.py": {
      "occurrences": 1,
      "branch": "origin/loop/iter7-external-tool-crosscheck",
      "why": "the MACHINE_PATHS list itself: one of the five shapes is its own literal"
    }
  },
